        "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2033}(x)$ for $f(x)={x}^{6}+{x}^{5}.$",
        "worked_solution": "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={({x}^{6}+{x}^{5})}^{\u2032} \\\\  & =6\\cdot {x}^{5}+5\\cdot {x}^{4} \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2033}(x) & ={(6{x}^{5}+5{x}^{4})}^{\u2032} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 6{x}^{4}+4\\cdot 5{x}^{3} \\\\  & =30{x}^{4}+20{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
